      "writtenOn": "2023-04-03T09:07:50Z",
      "side": 0,
      "message": "The `testGenerateHonorsRequestedAuthorizations` seems to indicate that StrongBox implementations *can* police supported HMAC digests on `generateKey`, but is that the same as saying they *have* to police supported HMAC digests on `generateKey`?\n\nI always get confused about whether KeyMint implementations are required-to or allowed-to police invalid key authorizations on `generateKey` or on use (`begin()`) -- there are other tests that allow for policing in either place (e.g. the `NoAttestKeyTest` CTS test).\n\nI agree that it would be nice if the HAL spec said what was allowed / required, but on a pragmatic level we can\u0027t require a change in behaviour for anything that\u0027s already passing xTS.\n\nSo I guess that comes back to the original question: could enabling this test for StrongBox potentially result in a VTS failure for a device that used to pass VTS?",
      "parentUuid": "46da677c_1d21d220",
      "revId": "a4ccb03efdd7824745cb0c62433065ef3f682346",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
